{"author":{"id":"8d2e0405f08ac6c481f912544d6d5c0f58b2dc14a7e51ad4d499ee7a34567943"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793793047,"nonce":"MaJEpz8Ch95EHuaTpgInqcUuvD8=","title":"staggered(direct=True) without a linear slot factorizes with spsolve, not the preferred direct backend","message":"With no `linear=` given, `staggered_newton` falls back to `sparse_lu_solve` (JAX `spsolve`), so on a GPU every block factorization is cuSolver's sparse QR even where cuDSS is installed. `lu()` with no backend picks cuDSS there (`_preferred_direct_backend`); staggered should resolve its default the same way. Also the solve's log line reports the default iterative slot (\"inner bicgstab (matrix-free) + jacobi\") although the direct path never uses it. Repro: a nonlinear two-field load-path march with `fem.solve(nonlinear=jno.solve.staggered([u, d], direct=True))` on a GPU, compared with the same call plus `linear=jno.solve.lu()`.","files":null}]}